WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.620
So I find that if you can trigger,
you know, you get things started by

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.820
listening in the morning, then you
just have to circle back later on.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.700
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.050
Today, I want to talk
about my morning routine.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.260
What do I do in the morning
to get my language learning

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.240
activities started for the day?

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.910
Remember if you enjoy these
videos, please subscribe click

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:22.980
on the bell for notifications.

00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:28.439
And if you follow these as podcasts
on Spotify or Apple Podcasts or

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:30.299
elsewhere, please leave a review.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.839
So people often ask me sort
of specifically, what do you

00:00:33.839 --> 00:00:36.030
do, uh, to learn the language?

00:00:36.089 --> 00:00:36.480
Okay.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.410
The morning is a big part
of my language learning day.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:45.510
Uh, if you can get stuff done in the
morning, first thing that kind of sets

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:50.865
you up for the day, uh, so that even
if it's not a very active day, from

00:00:50.865 --> 00:00:54.465
a language earning point of view, at
least you've taken that first step.

00:00:54.975 --> 00:01:01.665
So typically what I do in the morning,
you know, is, is I might, first of all,

00:01:01.695 --> 00:01:07.575
just kind of review a couple of lessons,
uh, on my iPad from the day before

00:01:07.575 --> 00:01:09.375
in whichever language I'm learning.

00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:11.385
And nowadays it's either
Arabic or Persian.

00:01:12.135 --> 00:01:14.535
But then okay, time to
get out of bed here.

00:01:14.925 --> 00:01:16.455
So yeah.

00:01:17.445 --> 00:01:21.405
I will set up in a room where it's quiet
and my wife doesn't have to listen to

00:01:21.405 --> 00:01:27.225
me, uh, where I will play something
that's easy to listen to, like the

00:01:27.225 --> 00:01:31.245
mini stories for example, even though
I've listened to them many times or

00:01:31.305 --> 00:01:34.575
something that's new and fresh, like
a podcast that I've just downloaded.

00:01:35.175 --> 00:01:38.055
So I'll put that on and that's
now running in the background.

00:01:38.685 --> 00:01:46.500
Then I go to my muscle booster, a website
where I have this seven minute routine.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.370
Okay.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:51.480
Which consists of sit ups and pushups
and burpees and stretching and,

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.500
and, uh, you know, side planks.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.150
And there's a range of things
and they mix them every day.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.980
I don't know what's coming at me next.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:03.150
It's all in 30 second intervals
and it's extremely good.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:08.264
But, and so for seven minutes, I will
be doing these exercises 30 seconds, 30

00:02:08.264 --> 00:02:14.025
seconds, 30 seconds while this, uh, Arabic
or Persian is running in the background.

00:02:14.445 --> 00:02:14.775
Okay.

00:02:15.165 --> 00:02:18.765
Then typically, if it's the summer,
now I go for a swim in the ocean

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:23.475
and the water is like 16, 17, 18
degrees, depending on the day.

00:02:23.715 --> 00:02:25.454
So that really wakes you up.

00:02:25.515 --> 00:02:29.265
I can tell you, uh, 16, I don't
know what that is in Fahrenheit.

00:02:29.475 --> 00:02:30.345
It's in the sixties.

00:02:30.345 --> 00:02:34.049
I think, uh, Around 60.

00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:38.790
So then, uh, time for breakfast.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.269
So typically I go in, I'll
cut up fruit, start preparing.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.709
We have muesli, uh, get, uh, you
know, I have to make some, uh, I

00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:51.329
make my espresso coffee, so I grind
some coffee beans set the table,

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.969
uh, and all the while I'm listening.

00:02:54.029 --> 00:02:54.660
Okay.

00:02:54.839 --> 00:03:00.029
If the dishwasher, uh, was full from
the night before we had just run the

00:03:00.029 --> 00:03:02.100
dishes, I'll go in and empty the dishes.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:07.980
Preparing for breakfast and then
also cleaning up after breakfast

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.080
is at least a half hour listening.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:16.110
Most days I will be doing that
activity and listening to my language.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:16.740
Okay.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:22.650
Now then maybe and it has been
the case that I tend to have my,

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:27.170
my Arabic online tutor sessions
around 10, 10.30 in the morning.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.700
And right now, uh, Mr.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.700
Mohammed seems to have disappeared
at iTalki so I have, um, Adel Samy.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.800
And so that, we'll have an hour
there, uh, two times a week.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.600
Uh, then very often my wife
likes to play golf, so we've

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.290
got golf set up at 12.30 or 1.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:47.870
So we charge off to the golf course.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.840
If I weren't in the car with my wife, I'd
be listening to Arabic or Persian, but you

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.340
can't, you know, there's a limit, right?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.000
There's a limit.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:56.600
I can't do that.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:02.970
Uh, so then when I come home, but I wanted
to focus on my morning routine because

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.190
now I have set myself up for the day.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:11.820
So when I come home, I need to find
another half hour or so maybe an hour to

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:17.519
sit down, to go through whatever it was
I listened to and save words and phrases

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:19.630
or review words, and phrases or read it.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.600
So that I basically pick up the pieces
from what I started in the morning,

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.940
but the morning is very important.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:33.090
First of all, the, the seven minute
exercise routine, which is great, um,

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:40.020
throwing myself in the water, sure
jars the brain cells, and then spending

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.330
some time, you know, with the language.

00:04:43.755 --> 00:04:46.875
Every so often I have to, you
know, vacuum or clean up or do

00:04:46.875 --> 00:04:48.255
other activities around the house.

00:04:48.345 --> 00:04:49.635
There again, I'll be listening.

00:04:49.635 --> 00:04:52.005
So a lot of that stuff
happens in the morning.

00:04:52.455 --> 00:04:56.745
Now other people have other
things happening in the morning.

00:04:56.745 --> 00:04:59.325
Like they might be going off to
work, but there again, there's an

00:04:59.325 --> 00:05:03.555
opportunity in a car or on a train
or a subway to listen to language.

00:05:03.885 --> 00:05:08.295
So I find that if you can trigger,
you know, or you get things started by

00:05:08.295 --> 00:05:13.275
listening in the morning, then you just
have to circle back later on and go

00:05:13.275 --> 00:05:17.114
and find those things you're listening
to where maybe you're curious about

00:05:17.114 --> 00:05:20.685
certain words or expressions that you
kind of half know, or completely don't

00:05:20.685 --> 00:05:25.215
know, and you can look them up and
start on the process of learning them.

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:28.905
So I just thought I'd mentioned
that my approach to the morning is,

00:05:29.114 --> 00:05:33.914
is to make that, you know, a place
to get a start on the day, whether

00:05:33.914 --> 00:05:34.965
it be through my physical action.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:39.630
If I have later, if I have time also with
the exercise, if I come home from the

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:44.750
golf and I have time, I might get on my,
a stepper or go for a run down at the

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:51.114
school yard or do something else, uh,
maybe lift some weights or use the TRX uh,

00:05:51.195 --> 00:05:52.664
you know, a band or something like that.

00:05:52.664 --> 00:05:56.445
But at least I've got in that seven
minutes of exercise in the morning.

00:05:56.715 --> 00:06:01.335
And also at least I've got in that half
an hour or 45 minutes combined listening

00:06:01.455 --> 00:06:05.745
in the morning to get a start on the day
from a language learning point of view.

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.724
So I hope that was of interest.

00:06:08.115 --> 00:06:09.945
And, uh, look forward to your comments.

